How to compile:

NV dependency:

1. Qt
2. Cairo
3. NCL

Here are some general info on how to get and install each piece:

1. Qt

	http://qt-project.org/

	(Wei uses Qt-4.7.4 (on Geyser, CSG installed 4.8).
		DONOT use Qt 5.0 or above, as there are some thing
		did not work for NV)

	The easiest way is downloading the binaries.

2. Cairo

	http://cairographics.org/

	(Wei uses 1.12.6)

	(The newest is 1.12.14)

	Wei's Cairo configure options:

#!/bin/csh -f

 setenv CC      gcc
 setenv CXX     g++
 setenv FC      gfortran

 setenv CAIRO_NO_MUTEX  1
 setenv HAS_PIXMAN_GLYPHS       0

 setenv pixman_CFLAGS   "-I/usr/local/pixman/0.26.2/include/pixman-1"
 setenv pixman_LIBS     "-L/usr/local/pixman/0.26.2/lib -lpixman-1"

#setenv qt_CFLAGS       "-pipe -g -gdwarf-2 -mmacosx-version-min=10.12 -DQT_GUI_LIB -DQT_CORE_LIB -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/mkspecs/default -I. -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib/QtCore.framework/Versions/4/Headers -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/include/QtCore -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib/QtGui.framework/Versions/4/Headers -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/include/QtGui -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/include -I. -F/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib"
#setenv qt_LIBS         "-F/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib -L/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib -framework QtGui -framework QtCore"

 setenv qt_CFLAGS       "-pipe -g -gdwarf-2 -mmacosx-version-min=10.12 -DQT_GUI_LIB -DQT_CORE_LIB -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/mkspecs/default -I. -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib/QtGui.framework/Versions/4/Headers -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/include/QtGui -I/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/include -I. -F/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib"
 setenv qt_LIBS         "-F/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib -L/Applications/Qt/Desktop/Qt/474/gcc/lib -framework QtGui"

 ./configure \
        --prefix=/Users/huangwei/ncl/external_lib/cairo/1.12.6 \
        --disable-shared \
        --enable-pthread=no \
        --enable-static \
        --enable-qt=yes \
        --enable-gl \
        --enable-png \
        --disable-quartz \
        --disable-quartz-font \
        --disable-silent-rules


NOTE: There are few executables are hard to generate.
	But since NCL nor NV use them, one can just do:
 touch ./test/any2ppm
 touch ./test/cairo-test-suite
 touch ./perf/cairo-analyse-trace
 touch ./perf/cairo-perf-trace
 touch ./perf/cairo-perf-micro
	to skip it.

