4. NV

a. configure

	just type "configure".

	This needs to be generalized, as now it works only for Wei's setup.

b. generate Makefile(s)

	type "qmake" to generate Makefile(s)

	This may contain something did not work on Mac.

I used a script (myqmake) to modify the generated Makefile

#!/bin/csh -f 

 qmake

 foreach f ( `find . -type f -name Makefile -print` )
    sed -e "s/-arch / /g" $f > tmp_file
    sed -e "s/-Xarch_x86_64 / /g" tmp_file > tmp2_file
    sed -e "s/x86_64 / /g" tmp2_file > $f
    rm -f tmp_file tmp2_file
 end


c. make

	(Or type "compile", if you have "myqmake" on your Mac)


